   "name": "What's Actually Inside a Car",
   "lines": [
    [
     "c02_1",
     {
      "label": "hook",
      "head": "What's *inside* your car?",
      "pose": "point",
      "face": "grin",
      "prop": {
       "type": "carmap",
       "hi": []
      }
     },
     "Let's strip a car down to the systems that actually make it work."
    ],
    [
     "c02_2",
     {
      "label": "engine",
      "head": "The *engine* makes the power",
      "pose": "present",
      "face": "smile",
      "prop": {
       "type": "carmap",
       "hi": [
        "engine",
        "radiator"
       ]
      }
     },
     "The engine, or the motor in an electric car, makes the power. The radiator keeps it from cooking itself."
    ],
    [
     "c02_3",
     {
      "label": "gearbox",
      "head": "The *gearbox* changes the ratio",
      "pose": "think",
      "face": "think",
      "prop": {
       "type": "carmap",
       "hi": [
        "gearbox"
       ]
      }
     },
     "The gearbox trades engine speed for pulling power, so you can pull away slowly or cruise fast."
    ],
    [
     "c02_4",
     {
      "label": "drivetrain",
      "head": "The *drivetrain* feeds the wheels",
      "pose": "present",
      "face": "smile",
      "prop": {
       "type": "carmap",
       "hi": [
        "shaft",
        "diff"
       ]
      }
     },
     "The driveshaft and differential carry that power to the driven wheels. This one is rear wheel drive."
    ],
    [
     "c02_5",
     {
      "label": "control",
      "head": "Steering, suspension, *brakes*",
      "pose": "count",
      "face": "smile",
      "prop": {
       "type": "carmap",
       "hi": [
        "steer",
        "susp",
        "brakes"
       ]
      }
     },
     "Steering points the wheels, suspension keeps the tyres on the road, and the brakes turn your speed into heat."
    ],
    [
     "c02_6",
     {
      "label": "chassis",
      "head": "The *body* holds it all together",
      "pose": "present",
      "face": "smug",
      "prop": {
       "type": "chassis",
       "mode": "mono"
      }
     },
     "The body shell ties everything together, and protects you in a crash."
    ],
    [
     "c02_7",
     {
      "label": "electrics",
      "head": "*Electrics* run everything else",
      "pose": "think",
      "face": "smile",
      "prop": {
       "type": "carmap",
       "hi": [
        "battery",
        "tank"
       ]
      }
     },
     "A battery starts the car, then the alternator keeps it charged, powering lights, sensors and dozens of small computers."
    ],
    [
     "c02_8",
     {
      "label": "takeaway",
      "head": "Six systems, *one* machine",
      "pose": "thumbs",
      "face": "grin",
